#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:5
#: 61c56886373140ad90925271c98a8a51
msgid "Internal Leak Failsafe"
msgstr "内部进水失控保护"

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:7
#: 4eec3ff384bd4ab6af004cd9eb006e33
msgid ""
"If sub is equipped with a leak detector internally, then a failsafe can "
"be enabled when a leak is detected. Sub provides the ability to have up "
"to three detectors. Each detector can be either analog or digital. When a"
" leak from any detector is detected, a failsafe can be enabled to occur."
msgstr "如果水下机器人内部装有进水检测器，则可在检测到进水时启用失控保护。水下机器人最多支持三个检测器，每个检测器可以是模拟或数字类型。当任意检测器检测到进水时，可启用相应的失控保护。"

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:9
#: ab8da4742a724a83a148135d60d9a3d3
msgid ""
"For the remainder of this article, the first leak detector's parameters "
"will used for example."
msgstr "本文其余部分将以第一个进水检测器的参数为例进行说明。"

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:12
#: b5e83b5e836643a18ba14edb9dc93134
msgid "When the failsafe will trigger"
msgstr "何时触发失控保护"

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:13
#: ce5567ad398f408ab7f9daf2c587448a
msgid ""
"If :ref:`FS_LEAK_ENABLE<FS_LEAK_ENABLE>` is non-zero, and a detector is "
"attached to either an analog input or GPIO pin on the autopilot, set by "
"the :ref:`LEAK1_PIN<LEAK1_PIN>`. Then if the detector is analog, it's "
"considered active (\"1\") if its voltage is > 2.0V. Digital sensors "
"present a normal digital logic level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:15
#: 4b5006167f4d46bcb3a2ef2080ae0de4
msgid ""
"Whether the active level of an analog sensor or the logic level from a "
"digital sensor is taken as \"dry\" is determined by the "
":ref:`LEAK1_LOGIC<LEAK1_LOGIC>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:17
#: 9852146b331a44668d16e2e8e8c8321e
msgid ""
"In ArduSub firmware prior or equal to 4.5, the input pin must be declared"
" to be analog or digital with the ``LEAKx_TYPE`` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:19
#: 961bfc6cc2134f1b973be7554ad9592d
msgid ""
"Digital leak detectors should be connected to digital input pins. Some "
"flight controllers support that on :ref:`servo channel ports <main-aux-"
"out>`, in which case the relevant channel(s) must be configured as :ref"
":`common-gpios`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:21
#: bb86c2e018fe467983198799bf9e4e01
msgid ""
"Leak detections can also be triggered from a MAVLink subsystem (matching "
"the autopilot's MAVLink system ID), via the extended form of `SYS_STATUS "
"<https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#SYS_STATUS>`__ messages. This"
" can be useful for \"remote\" leak detection (e.g. in a separate "
"enclosure to the autopilot), where it may be impractical to run a leak "
"sensor probe to, or if the autopilot does not have enough GPIO pins "
"available for the desired number of probes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:24
#: 7cd89d3bcf67470fb0e5ea8f0ebf8028
msgid "What will happen"
msgstr "将会发生什么"

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:25
#: 69831c5d48344c53b2c2f3cee28ae6eb
msgid ""
"When the failsafe occurs, the action taken is determined by the value of "
":ref:`FS_LEAK_ENABLE<FS_LEAK_ENABLE>`:"
msgstr "失控保护触发时，采取的动作由 :ref:`FS_LEAK_ENABLE<FS_LEAK_ENABLE>` 的值决定："

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:27
#: 5176ee1c20c14f17b2d2e4413db836c3
msgid "**Disabled** (Value 0) will disable the failsafe entirely."
msgstr "**禁用** （值 0）将完全禁用失控保护。"

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:28
#: 042362c87d1a462dbd600cff08594d65
#, fuzzy
msgid "**Warn Only** (Value 1) will send a \"Leak Detected\" GCS warning message."
msgstr "**仅警告** （值 1）将向地面站发送警告消息。"

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:29
#: 0e82a3e1f0914e8cb98c3b7881f1afa2
msgid ""
"On a flight controller with notifying hardware, status LEDs will flash "
"yellow and white, and the buzzer will play a cycle of falling tones"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/internal-leak-failsafe.rst:30
#: a97c2f09d726449cadb75bece6b31fda
msgid ""
"**Enter SURFACE Mode** (Value 2) will send a warning and return the "
"vehicle to the surface."
msgstr ""

